{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/439445-tribe-propreitary-gifts","id":439445,"title":"Tribe Propreitary Gifts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-12T23:03:48-07:00","id":439445,"title":"Tribe Propreitary Gifts","content":"I like the Tribal Merits, but I also personally would enjoy the Tribes having Gifts that are truly their exclusive playground. Obviously the system is now geared toward stopping redundancies, and since all Gift Facets are roughly equally leveled, that closes a lot of area that Battle, Ending, Stalking, Blending, and Alpha Gifts covered previously (since many of their powers were differently scaled effects similar to areas other Gifts covered).<br /> <br /> I do have some ideas though...<br /> <br /> Stalking (Gift of Black Wolf) would be perhaps the easiest to translate, pulling on Darkness to fill in some of the blanks. &quot;Shadow Pack&quot; (Purity) can fill the hole &quot;Spirit Pack&quot; left, and we can just make the shadow wolves more fragile and fleeting (as befits shadows) to tone down the power-level to Gift Facet level. Leaping into one shadow and out another is a somewhat obvious (Cunning) facet. Etc.<br /> <br /> My idea for Adaptation (Gift of Red Wolf) is facets that allow the Iron Master to take on the physical properties of different substances through physical contact.<br /> <br /> Honor: Take on the flexibility and strength (and sheen) of metal.<br /> Glory: The hardness of stone<br /> Wisdom: The growing properties of wood<br /> Purity: the fluidity of water or sand<br /> Cunning: Assume &quot;perfect&quot; humanity, suppressing abilities and drawbacks of being a werewolf for a window of time<br /> <br /> <br /> Not sure on the others yet, but a Gift aimed specifically at resisting supernatural powers and influence is obviously fitting for Winter Wolf's Gift to the Storm Lords.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T04:02:40-07:00","id":439705,"title":"","content":"All Tribes have one exclusive Gift they only have:<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Talons:</b> Rage<br /> <br /> <b>Bone Shadows:</b> Death<br /> <br /> <b>Hunters in Darkness:</b> Nature<br /> <br /> <b>Iron Masters:</b> Technology<br /> <br /> <b>Storm Lords:</b> Weather<br /> <br /> What do you want is perhaps a Tribe Gift similar to the Auspice ones?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T04:09:26-07:00","id":439709,"title":"","content":"Those are gifts they alone favor, not ones that are exclusive to them. Any Werewolf can start the game with any of those Gifts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T04:39:32-07:00","id":439728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/439445-tribe-propreitary-gifts?p=439709#post439709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those are gifts they alone favor, not ones that are exclusive to them. Any Werewolf can start the game with any of those Gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Only if you spend 5 experiences in chargen to buy them. Otherwise, you have to pick your Gifts from your Auspice and Tribe lists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T05:13:00-07:00","id":439780,"title":"","content":"The five Shadow Gifts that are uniquely favoured by a given Tribe cannot be accessed at character creation unless you've doled out more Experiences for them to start with, since your starting Shadow picks have to come from the Gifts favoured by your Auspice and Tribe.<br /> <br /> However, once the game is up and running, Rage, Death, Nature, Technology and Weather can all be accessed by werewolves outside of those respective Tribes, albeit at the premium Experience cost for a non-favoured Gift - and, obviously, requiring you to find a spirit that will teach them and getting carved up by that spirit <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> One of my specific design approaches for Shadow Gifts in this edition was that there is essentially no such thing as the genuinely exclusive 'proprietary' Shadow Gift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T06:16:21-07:00","id":439821,"title":"","content":"The thing with Shadow gifts is you're supposed to be able to get them after a successful Siskur-Dah from a spirit. A proprietary gift set would cancel that with certain spirits or gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T06:48:06-07:00","id":439835,"title":"","content":"I'd still love it if someone could come up with an Alpha list...pwetty pwease?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3777-the-scorpion","name":"The Scorpion","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T10:58:57-07:00","id":440149,"title":"","content":"With an Alpha gift set, I could see Glory adding to Presence by Renown. Maybe Honor would detract from penalties regarding socialization due to being an Uratha.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T11:09:20-07:00","id":440166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/439445-tribe-propreitary-gifts?p=440149#post440149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With an Alpha gift set, I could see Glory adding to Presence by Renown. Maybe Honor would detract from penalties regarding socialization due to being an Uratha.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are no such social handicaps anymore, that I've seen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T11:13:16-07:00","id":440169,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/439445-tribe-propreitary-gifts?p=440166#post440166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are no such social handicaps anymore, that I've seen.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 'Most spirits have average or hostile first impressions with the Forsaken,' but it could also work to deal with things like idigam, hosts, the claimed, and so forth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T12:35:12-07:00","id":440303,"title":"","content":"I refer to the negative modifiers to social rolls that don't involve intimidation with normal people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T12:37:13-07:00","id":440306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thorbes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/439445-tribe-propreitary-gifts?p=439705#post439705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All Tribes have one exclusive Gift they only have:<br /> <br /> <b>Blood Talons:</b> Rage<br /> <br /> <b>Bone Shadows:</b> Death<br /> <br /> <b>Hunters in Darkness:</b> Nature<br /> <br /> <b>Iron Masters:</b> Technology<br /> <br /> <b>Storm Lords:</b> Weather<br /> <br /> What do you want is perhaps a Tribe Gift similar to the Auspice ones?</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooh, I like this idea.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T12:40:47-07:00","id":440310,"title":"","content":"I use a &quot;Prey&quot; gift in my system. It'sactually 5 different gifts, one for each tribe, whose purpose is helping you hunt the tribe's respective Prey. You can't learn Prey (Hosts) if you're not a Hunter in Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/286-christian-a","name":"Christian A","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"832"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-13T13:57:12-07:00","id":440442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Christian A</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/439445-tribe-propreitary-gifts?p=440310#post440310\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I use a &quot;Prey&quot; gift in my system. It'sactually 5 different gifts, one for each tribe, whose purpose is helping you hunt the tribe's respective Prey. You can't learn Prey (Hosts) if you're not a Hunter in Darkness.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be fucking amazing.<br /> <br /> All the damned Tribes scouring the Shadow in search of Prey (Idigam) gifts.<br /> <br /> I'd call them Prey Upon (#antagonist).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}